            <trans-unit id="forecast_import.guide.intro">
                <source>forecast_import.guide.intro</source>
                <target>The import copies your team's plan from Harvest Forecast into the Weekly Planner, so nobody has to type the coming months in again. It works in five steps. Only the last one writes anything, and you can go back to any step at any time.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="forecast_import.guide.read_title">
                <source>forecast_import.guide.read_title</source>
                <target>Read Forecast</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="forecast_import.guide.read">
                <source>forecast_import.guide.read</source>
                <target>Enter your Forecast account ID and a Harvest personal access token. The import reads people, projects and planning for the dates you choose and keeps a copy for the next steps. Nothing is imported yet. The token is only kept if you tick "Remember", and then encrypted; clear it once you have finished importing.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="forecast_import.guide.people_title">
                <source>forecast_import.guide.people_title</source>
                <target>People</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="forecast_import.guide.people">
                <source>forecast_import.guide.people</source>
                <target>Each Forecast person is matched to the Kimai user with the same email address, marked "Automatic". Change any match, or choose not to import someone's planning. Placeholders are skipped, because the planner plans people, but you can give one to a user.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="forecast_import.guide.projects_title">
                <source>forecast_import.guide.projects_title</source>
                <target>Projects</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="forecast_import.guide.projects">
                <source>forecast_import.guide.projects</source>
                <target>Project names rarely match exactly between Forecast and Kimai, so the import suggests the closest Kimai project by comparing customer and project names. Strong suggestions are ticked: accept them in one go, then decide the rest. A Forecast project can go to a customer without a project, become time off, or be left out. Forecast's "Time Off" project becomes time off by itself.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="forecast_import.guide.tentative_title">
                <source>forecast_import.guide.tentative_title</source>
                <target>Tentative work</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="forecast_import.guide.tentative">
                <source>forecast_import.guide.tentative</source>
                <target>Forecast has no tentative flag. If you tag projects that are not signed yet, choose those tags here and their planning arrives as tentative planning.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="forecast_import.guide.preview_title">
                <source>forecast_import.guide.preview_title</source>
                <target>Preview and import</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="forecast_import.guide.preview">
                <source>forecast_import.guide.preview</source>
                <target>See exactly what the import would do, per person: what is new, what changed in Forecast, what will be removed and what is already up to date, plus anything left out and why. Nothing is written until you press "Import planning".</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="forecast_import.guide.again_title">
                <source>forecast_import.guide.again_title</source>
                <target>Running it again</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="forecast_import.guide.again">
                <source>forecast_import.guide.again</source>
                <target>Until you switch Forecast off, repeat it whenever Forecast changes: read Forecast again, map anything new, preview, import. Each planning remembers where it came from, so nothing is created twice and plans that did not change are left alone.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="forecast_import.guide.expect_title">
                <source>forecast_import.guide.expect_title</source>
                <target>What to expect</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="forecast_import.guide.expect_days">
                <source>forecast_import.guide.expect_days</source>
                <target>Forecast books working days only. Plannings are cut around each person's days off and public holidays, so a booking from Thursday to Tuesday arrives as Thursday to Friday and Monday to Tuesday.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="forecast_import.guide.expect_hours">
                <source>forecast_import.guide.expect_hours</source>
                <target>Hours per day come straight from Forecast. Time off without hours becomes a whole day off.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="forecast_import.guide.expect_time_off">
                <source>forecast_import.guide.expect_time_off</source>
                <target>Time off reduces a person's capacity in the planner instead of counting as planned work.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="forecast_import.guide.expect_range">
                <source>forecast_import.guide.expect_range</source>
                <target>Only the dates you read are touched. Nothing before the start date is created or changed.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="forecast_import.guide.expect_edits">
                <source>forecast_import.guide.expect_edits</source>
                <target>Changes made in Kimai to an imported planning stay until the same assignment changes in Forecast. Then Forecast wins, because it is still the source until you switch it off.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="forecast_import.guide.expect_not">
                <source>forecast_import.guide.expect_not</source>
                <target>Milestones, budgets and roles in Forecast are not imported. "Start over" removes every imported planning if you want a clean slate; your mapping decisions are kept.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="forecast_import.range_changed">
                <source>forecast_import.range_changed</source>
                <target>The dates differ from the previous read, so only the days both reads cover are compared.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="forecast_import.problem.no_work_contract">
                <source>forecast_import.problem.no_work_contract</source>
                <target>No working days in the Kimai work contract, so Forecast's working days were used</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="forecast_import.status">
                <source>forecast_import.status</source>
                <target>Status</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="forecast_import.status_imported">
                <source>forecast_import.status_imported</source>
                <target>Mapped for import</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="forecast_import.status_time_off">
                <source>forecast_import.status_time_off</source>
                <target>Mapped as time off</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="forecast_import.status_skipped">
                <source>forecast_import.status_skipped</source>
                <target>Excluded from import</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="forecast_import.status_skipped_help">
                <source>forecast_import.status_skipped_help</source>
                <target>You chose not to import this. Change it to include it after all.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="forecast_import.status_skipped_default_help">
                <source>forecast_import.status_skipped_default_help</source>
                <target>Placeholders are not imported unless you give them to a user.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="forecast_import.status_left_out">
                <source>forecast_import.status_left_out</source>
                <target>Not mapped yet</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="forecast_import.status_left_out_help">
                <source>forecast_import.status_left_out_help</source>
                <target>Nothing is imported for this until you decide where it goes in Kimai. Whatever an earlier import created for it stays.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="forecast_import.guide.skip_title">
                <source>forecast_import.guide.skip_title</source>
                <target>Choosing not to import</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="forecast_import.guide.skip">
                <source>forecast_import.guide.skip</source>
                <target>Choose "Do not import" for a person or a project and none of its Forecast planning is imported. If an earlier import already created plannings for it, the next import removes them, within the import dates. Plannings made in Kimai are never touched, and you can change your mind at any time: the next import brings the planning in again. Something not mapped yet is different: it is simply left out, and whatever an earlier import created for it stays.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="forecast_import.action_help_person">
                <source>forecast_import.action_help_person</source>
                <target>Not importing a person leaves out all of their Forecast planning, and the next import removes what an earlier one created for them.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="forecast_import.action_help_project">
                <source>forecast_import.action_help_project</source>
                <target>Not importing a project leaves out all of its Forecast planning, and the next import removes what an earlier one created for it.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="forecast_import.col_person">
                <source>forecast_import.col_person</source>
                <target>Person in Forecast</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="forecast_import.col_project">
                <source>forecast_import.col_project</source>
                <target>Project in Forecast</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="forecast_import.col_planned">
                <source>forecast_import.col_planned</source>
                <target>Planned in Forecast</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="forecast_import.col_goes_to">
                <source>forecast_import.col_goes_to</source>
                <target>Goes to in Kimai</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="forecast_import.planned_hours">
                <source>forecast_import.planned_hours</source>
                <target>≈ %hours% h</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="forecast_import.planned_days">
                <source>forecast_import.planned_days</source>
                <target>{1} 1 whole day|]1,Inf[ %count% whole days</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="forecast_import.bookings">
                <source>forecast_import.bookings</source>
                <target>{1} 1 booking|]1,Inf[ %count% bookings</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="forecast_import.problem.for_everyone">
                <source>forecast_import.problem.for_everyone</source>
                <target>Days off Forecast gives everyone at once. They are not imported: set them as public holidays in the planner instead</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="forecast_import.token_help_saved">
                <source>forecast_import.token_help_saved</source>
                <target>A saved token is used when you leave this empty. Type a new one to replace it.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="forecast_import.remember_token">
                <source>forecast_import.remember_token</source>
                <target>Remember the token for the next read</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="forecast_import.remember_token_help">
                <source>forecast_import.remember_token_help</source>
                <target>Kept encrypted with this Kimai's secret key, and only after Forecast has accepted it. Clear it when you are done.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="forecast_import.token_needed">
                <source>forecast_import.token_needed</source>
                <target>Enter a token: none is saved for this account.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="forecast_import.token_saved_notice">
                <source>forecast_import.token_saved_notice</source>
                <target>A token for account %account% is saved, encrypted, since %date%.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="forecast_import.clear_token">
                <source>forecast_import.clear_token</source>
                <target>Clear saved token</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="forecast_import.clear_after_import">
                <source>forecast_import.clear_after_import</source>
                <target>A Harvest token is still saved. Clear it unless you plan to import again: a token in Kimai is a key to your Forecast account.</target>
            </trans-unit>
        </body>
